course: dictionary
lesson: 6263
title: Mom, Mum or Mam: Words for mother
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Mom is an informal word for your mother. People in the USA and Canada use it most. When you call to your mother, you might say, «Mom, can I go out?»
explain: Context tells you who is meant. In «Josh in Pittsburgh told Mom his brother had called him a bad name», Mom is Josh's mother, because he is telling her about a problem at home. Look for clues like the place, the family words around it and what happens.
explain: The same person has different words in different places. In Britain and Australia people say Mum, and in Ireland some people say Mam. When you read a story from another country, check where it is set and what the characters call their mother.
fact: Mom is an informal word for mother, used mainly in the USA and Canada.
fact: You can use Mom as a name when you talk to your mother: «Mom, can I go out?»
fact: In the UK, Australia and New Zealand, people usually say Mum instead.
fact: In Ireland, people may say Mam.
fact: «Mom and Dad» means your mother and your father together.
exercise: «Josh in Pittsburgh told Mom his brother had called him a bad name.» Who is Mom? | *Josh's mother | A friend from school | Josh's teacher | Josh's brother
exercise: Which word do people in the UK and Australia usually use instead of Mom? | *Mum | Mama-Bear | Ma | Madam
exercise: Mom is an informal word. Which country is it used in most? | Ireland only | *Canada | Scotland | Wales
test: In «Mom, can I go out?», what is Mom? | A kind of dog | A street in town | A petrol station | *A name you call your mother
test: Mom means the same as which word? | Grandad | *Mother | Sister | Father
exam: Which word would a child in Canada most likely use to call their mother? | Mother | *Mom | Madam | Mammal
